Neon spaces (M3), part 4 of 4: range selection and keyboard moves.

Shift-click range selection took every tab between the two clicked tabs in
model order, so a range from a pinned to an unpinned tab took in other
spaces' tabs. Moving a tab with Ctrl+Shift+PgDn or PgUp could step into
another space's tabs. TabStripModel::GetTabRange, used only for selection ranges, now drops
hidden tabs, and MoveTabRelative stops at a hidden neighbour.

--- a/chrome/browser/ui/tabs/tab_strip_model.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/tabs/tab_strip_model.cc
